$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Compound 9. Phthalimide (11 g, 75.6 mmol) was dissolved in
80 ml of DMSO under argon inert gas atmosphere. After addition of K2CO3
(20 g, 144 mmol), the reaction mixture was heated for 2 hours at 120°C.
Subsequently, the reaction mixture was cooled to about 50°C, and p-bromo
benzyl bromide (18 g, 72 mmol) was added. After stirring for another 10
hours, 100 ml H2O was added. The colourless precipitate was filtered,
washed and dried. (18.6 g) yield 82%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 4.77 (s,
2H, NCH2), 7.29 (d, J=8.4 Hz, 2H, ArH), 7.41 (d, J=8.4 Hz, 2H, ArH),
7.67-7.70 (m, 2H, ArH), 7.80-7.83 (m, 2H, ArH); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz):
δ 40.9, 121.8, 123.3 (2C), 130.3 (2C), 131.7 (2C), 131.9 (2C), 134.0
(2C), 135.2, 167.8 (2C); MS (FAB): M+ = 315, found: 316 (M++1), 318
(M++3); IR (Film, cm-1) νmax = 3460, 3100, 3045, 2938, 1771, 1702, 1612,
1486, 1464, 1430, 1399, 1332, 1298, 1173, 1077, 1010, 957, 935, 845, 796,
731, 713, 528.
