$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N-protected N-alkyl ethyl oxamates 2. General
procedure: To a solution of 1 (3 mmol) in dry DMF (5 mL) was added
potassium t-butoxide (336 mg, 3 mmol) and bromide reagent (2.3 mmol). The
solution was heated at 60 °C for 1 h. After addition of CH2Cl2 (10 mL) to
the mixture, the organic layer was washed with water (2x10 mL), dried
over sodium sulfate and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel using
ethylacetate/cyclohexane (1/4) as eluent and gave 2a-f.
N-t-butoxycarbonyl N-prop-2-enyl ethyl oxamate 2d, yield 94%. 1H NMR δ
1.28 (t, J 7, 3H); 1.43 (s, 9H); 4.17-4.19 (dxt, 2J 1.4, 3J 5.6, 2H);
4.27 (q, J 7, 2H); 5.09-5.17 (m, 2H); 5.69-5.78 (m, 1H); 13C NMR δ 13.49;
27.41; 44.70 ; 61.75; 84.81; 117.18; 131.34; 151.16; 161.45; 162.66. HRMS
calcd for C12H19NO5: 257.1263 (M+); found: 257.1263.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Boc and N-Cbz ethyl oxamates: new Gabriel reagents
