$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Farnesylphthalimide (lb); Typical Procedure: DIAD (115 μL, 0.585 mmol)
was added dropwise in the dark to a solution of farnesol (1a; 100mg, 0.45
mmol), phthalimide (86 mg, 0.58 mmol), and Ph3P (153 mg, 0.58 mmol) in
anhydr. THF (5 mL) at r. t. After stirring the mixture for 4 h, H2O (20
mL) was added and the aqueous phase was extracted with hexane (3 x 15
mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried (MgSO4),
and filtered. The filtrate was evaporated in vacuo and the resulting
residue applied to a 2 x 13 cm silica gel column. Flash chromatography
using 1 % EtOAc/hexane provided N-farnesylphthalimide (1b). Colorless
oil, yield 147 mg, 93 %. IR (neat/KBr) v (cm-1): 2923,1712; 1H NMR
(CDCl3/TMS) δ, J (Hz): 7.8 (m, 2H, ArH), 7.7 (m, 2H, ArH), 5.27 (t, 1H,
C=CH, J= 7), 5.05 (m, 2H, 2C=CH), 4.27 (d, 2H, CH2N, J= 7), 2.00 (m, 8H,
C=CCH2), 1.83 (s, 3 H, CH3), 1.66 (s, 3 H, CH3), 1.56 (s, 6 H, 2 CH3);
13C NMR (CDCl3/TMS) δ: 168.0, 140.6, 135.3, 133.6, 132.4, 131.1, 124.3,
123.6, 123.0, 118.0, 39.6, 39.4, 35.8, 26.7, 26.2, 25.6, 17.6, 16.3,
15.9.
