$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Benzyl N,N-di-Boc-glycinate (BoC2-GIy-OBzl, 5): A vigorously stirred
suspension of fine-grained, thorougily dried potassium salt of 3 (2:5.5
g, 0.10 mol) in dry dimethylformanide (150 ml) is slowly treated with
benzyl bromoacetate (23.4 g, 0.102 mol), dissolved in dry
dimethylformamidc (100 ml). The resulting light-yellow slurry becomes
lukewarm and the stirring is continued for 10 h at 40 °C. Most of the
solvent is stripped off in vacuo and the semisolid yellowish residue is
worked up as described above for compound 4. The resulting ethereal
extract is treated with decolourizing carbon and the filtrate is
evaporated to complete dryness at reduced pressure below 40 °C to afford
crude 5.1H-NMR of the product reveals the presence of 3 and benzyl
brornoacetate (~2% of each). Recrystallization from petroleum ether gives
pure 5, identical with that obtained earlier. Colourless oil, yield 34.1
g 93%. m.p. 28-29°C. C19H27NO6 (365.4);calc. C 62.4 H 7.5 N 3.8 found
62.3 7.9 3.8; 1H-NMR (CD3CN/TMS): δ 1.43 (s, 18 H); 4.32 (s, 2 H); 5.16
(s, 2 H); 7.37 pprn (s, 5 H).
