$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of compound 19. Compound 18 (16 g, 53.9 mmol), phthalimide
(10.3 g, 72 mmol) and K2CO3 (9.7 g, 72 mmol) were heated in 60 ml of dry
acetone for 12 h under reflux. Thereafter, the acetone was distilled
under reduced pressure, and 100 ml of water was added to dissolve the
inorganic salts. The reaction mixture was filtered under reduced
pressure, washed with water and dried, which gave compound 19. (17.6 g)
as a white solid. Yield was 90%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 1.31 (s, 12H,
4CH3), 4.85 (s, 2H, CH2), 7.42 (d, J= 6.6 Hz, 2H, ArH), 7.67-7.70 (m, 2H,
ArH), 7.76 (d, J= 6.6 Hz, 2H, ArH), 7.81-7.84 (m, 2H, ArH); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 24.8 (4C), 41.6, 83.7 (2C), 123.3 (2C), 127.8 (2C),
132.1, 133.9 (2C), 135.1 (3C), 139.3 (2C), 167.9 (2C); MS (EI): m/z (%):
363 (M+, 100), 348 (17), 264 (37), 217 (34), 160 (31), 130 (29), 117
(92), 91 (16), 76 (36), 43 (78); IR (Film, cm-1) νmax = 2989, 2941, 1772,
1718, 1610, 1429, 1393, 1358, 1342, 1141, 1087, 1020, 962, 938, 856, 786,
718, 659.
