$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-protected N-alkyl ethyl oxamates 2. General procedure: To a solution of
1 (3 mmol) in dry DMF (5 mL) was added potassium t-butoxide (336 mg, 3
mmol) and bromide reagent (2.3 mmol). The solution was heated at 60 °C
for 1 h. After addition of CH2Cl2 (10 mL) to the mixture, the organic
layer was washed with water (2x10 mL), dried over sodium sulfate and the
solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel using ethylacetate/cyclohexane (1/4) as
eluent and gave 2a-f. N-t-butoxycarbonyl N-ethylacetate ethyl oxamate 2a,
yield 89%. 1H NMR δ 1.43 (t, J 7, 3H); 1.52 (t, J 7, 3H); 1.65 (s, 9H);
4.37 (q, J 7, 2H); 4.51 (q, J 7, 2H); 4.54 (s, 2H); 13C NMR δ 14.10;
14.42; 27.96; 58.58; 44.08; 61.95 ; 62.60; 86.18; 151.06; 161.60; 163.14;
167.77. HRMS calcd for C9H12NO7 246.0614 (M+ - C4H9); found: 246.0618.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Boc and N-Cbz ethyl oxamates: new Gabriel reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Berree, Fabienne; Bazureau, Jean-Pierre; Michelot, Gwendal; Le Corre,
Maurice
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1999), 29(15), 2685-2693

