$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.3 Synthesis of
2-[3-(2-nitrophenoxy)-propyl]isoindoline-1,3-dione (4a)[10] 1.0 g (0.005
mol) 3-(2-nitrophenoxy)-1-propylbromide (3a), 0.92 g (0.0051 mol)
phthalimide potassium and DMF (30 mL) were added into a reaction flask.
The reaction was stirred at 95 °C for 3 h. The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature followed by the addition of 80 mL water. The
solution was extracted with chloroform (40 mL × 4). The chloroform layer
was first washed with 0.2 mol/L NaOH solution (40 mL × 2) then water (30
mL × 2), dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate and concentrated under
reduced pressure until a crystal precipitated. Ethyl ether (50 mL) was
added for dispersion and the crystal separated out. The mixture solution
was filtered, and the resulting product dried to give 2-[3-
(2-nitrophenoxy)-propyl]isoindoline-1,3-dione (4a) as an off-white
crystal (0.91 g, yield 73 %).
2-[3-(4-chloro-2-nitrophenoxy)-propyl]isoindoline-1,3-dione (4d), 85 %
m.p. 175-177 °C, 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ: 7.84-7.81 (m, 3H, Ar-H), 7.72-7.70 (m,
2H, Ar-H), 7.46 (dd, J = 6.3, 2.6 Hz, 1H, 5-Ar-H), 7.01 (d, J = 9.0 Hz,
1H, 6-Ar-H), 4.16 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H, 3-CH2), 3.93 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 2H,
1-CH2), 2.26-2.22 (m, 2H, 2-CH2); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ: 168.5,
151.1, 140.2, 134.1, 134.0, 132.3, 125.7, 125.7, 123.4, 116.2, 68.1,
