$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: To a solution of 2 (2 mmol)
in THF (4 mL) was added a solution of LiOH (6 mmol) in H2O (3 mL) at room
temperature. After 3 h, the reaction mixture was diluted with H2O and
extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was dried over sodium sulfate
and concentrated in vacuo to give 3. General procedure: To a solution of
1 (3 mmol) in dry DMF (5 mL) was added potassium t-butoxide (336 mg, 3
mmol) and bromide reagent (2.3 mmol). The solution was heated at 60 °C
for 1 h. After addition of CH2Cl2 (10 mL) to the mixture, the organic
layer was washed with water (2x10 mL), dried over sodium sulfate and the
solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel using ethylacetate/cyclohexane (1/4) as
eluent and gave 2a-f. N-t-butoxycarbonyl pyrrolidine 57 : This compound
was obtained in 75 % yield from 3e (504 mg, 2 mmol) by using the
conditions described for the preparation of the oxamates 2. 1H NMR δ 1.36
(s,9H); 1.65-1.81 (m, 4H); 3.20 (t, J 7, 4H); 13C NMR δ 24.79; 25.54;
28.33; 45.41; 45.73; 78.64; 154.47.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
