$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.3 Synthesis of 2-[3-(2-nitrophenoxy)-propyl]isoindoline-1,3-dione
(4a)[10] 1.0 g (0.005 mol) 3-(2-nitrophenoxy)-1-propylbromide (3a), 0.92
g (0.0051 mol) phthalimide potassium and DMF (30 mL) were added into a
reaction flask. The reaction was stirred at 95 °C for 3 h. The reaction
mixture was cooled to room temperature followed by the addition of 80 mL
water. The solution was extracted with chloroform (40 mL × 4). The
chloroform layer was first washed with 0.2 mol/L NaOH solution (40 mL ×
2) then water (30 mL × 2), dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate and
concentrated under reduced pressure until a crystal precipitated. Ethyl
ether (50 mL) was added for dispersion and the crystal separated out. The
mixture solution was filtered, and the resulting product dried to give
2-[3- (2-nitrophenoxy)-propyl]isoindoline-1,3-dione (4a) as an off-white
crystal (0.91 g, yield 73 %).
2-[3-(2-nitrophenoxy)-propyl]isoindoline-1,3-dione (4a), 73 %, off-white
crystal m.p. 162-164 °C (literature value[10]: 163-165 °C), 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ: 7.83-7.81 (m, 3H, Ar-H), 7.71-7.69 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.53-7.48
(m, 1H, Ar-H), 7.07-7.01 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 4.17 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H, 3-CH2),
3.94 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H, 1-CH2), 2.27-2.22 (m, 2H, 2-CH2); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75.5 MHz) δ: 168.4, 152.3, 140.1, 134.2, 134.0, 132.2, 125.8,
123.3, 120.6, 114.8, 67.6, 35.3, 28.5; FTIR (KBr) ν: 1767, 1712, 1607,
1520, 1377, 1338, 1280, 1060, 1027 cm-1. Anal. calcd for C17H14N2O5: C
62.57, H 4.32, N 8.59; found C 62.61, H 4.33, N 8.67; MS (EI) m/z (%):
188 (40.26), 160 (100).
