$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Synthetic Procedures for II. To a
solution of I (6 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (10 mL) was added
potassium phthalimide (6 mmol) in portions. After the mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 5 h, water (50 mL) was added, and the precipitate
was collected by filtration and washed with water. After
recrystallization from ethanol, A white crystal was obtained. II4. Yield,
71.9%; mp, 138- 140 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 2.27 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.94 (s, 2H,
CH2), 6.64 (s, 1H, Ar-H), 7.74-7.77 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.89-7.92 (m, 2H,
Ar-H).
