$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Diethyl
N-Alkyl-N-(t-butoxycarbonyl)-phosphoramidates (6); General Procedure: A
mixture of sodium derivative 4 (5.50 g, 0.02 mol), the alkyl bromide (5;
0.02 mol), tetrabutylaminium bromide (0.64 g, 0.002 mol), and benzene (25
ml) is refluxed with stirring for 3 h. The product is cooled to room
temperature, diluted with benzene (25 ml), and treated with water (10 ml)
to dissolve sodium bromide. The organic layer is separated and washed
with water (3 × 10 ml). The washings are reextracted with benzene (3 × 10
ml) and the extracts arc combined with the organic layer. The extract is
dried with magnesium sulfate and evaporated and the residue heated at
30-40 °C/1-2 torr for 1 h to give either spectroscopically pure (1H- and
31P-N.M.R.) 6 (a-i) or 6 (j, k, l) contaminated with unreacted 3. Diethyl
N-Alkyl-N-(t-butoxycarbonyl)-phosphoramidates (6k). Yield: 36%. The
reaction was carried out in boiling acetonitrile for 6 h. The product was
isolated after evaporation of acetonitrile and replacing it by benzene.
As determined by 31P-N.M.R. spectrometry, the crude product is a mixture
of 6k (69%) and 3 (31%). 31P-N.M.R. 24.3 MHz (CCl4/85% H3PO4ext): δ
[ppm]: 0.20.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diethyl N-(tert-butoxycarbonyl)phosphoramidate: a new, useful substitute
of phthalimide in Gabriel-type syntheses of primary amines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zwierzak, Andrzej; Pilichowska, Slawomira
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1982), (11), 922-4

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME196 STEP1
